<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Wild at Heart</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;"It will be universally admitted that instincts are as important as corporeal structures for the welfare of each species, under their present conditions of life. Under changed conditions, it is at least possible that slight modifications of instinct might be profitable. For it is not the strongest that survives, nor the most intelligent, but the one most responsive to change."&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When speaking of adaptability, Catra has always found a way no matter what in order to survive. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following her instincts has been a crucial part to ensure that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;...she never would have thought that one day she'd have to surrender to them though. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fortunately enough, she doesn't have to do it alone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Or,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When dealing with perpetual changes, Adora has always been Catra's constant.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>TheWillOfMythal</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
